Javier Aránega and David Boceta's installation converts Lorca's "Oda a Salvador Dalí" into an interactive sound piece: David Boceta's voice recites the poem while the audience's movements modify the sound in real time, turning poetry into a live, participatory experience.

I built the heart rate sensor system that connects to Javier's audio generation engine, letting it read participants' real-time heart rate as an input to the piece.

Shown as part of "Lorca en Cataluña: Yo no he nacido todavía," curated by Francisco Ortuño Millán for Art Hub Collective, Venice 2026 at the Venice Biennale.

More information : [Art Hub Collective](https://www.arthubcollective.art/lorca)

Link to artist's presentation : [https://youtu.be/pfvH1bdk39o](https://youtu.be/pfvH1bdk39o)
